Q: Kibana: Use timestamp from log file instead of @timestamp A: <p>I had a similar problem for the same log pattern "2014-10-31 02:45:09,355". This configuration worked for me.</p>

<pre><code>grok {
    match =&gt; [ "message", "%{DATESTAMP:timestamp}" ]
}
date {
    locale =&gt; "en"
    timezone =&gt; "Europe/Paris"
    match =&gt; [ "timestamp", "yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss,SSS" ]
    target =&gt; ["tstamp"]
    remove_field =&gt; ["timestamp"]
}
</code></pre>
